<title>USA: TABLE - Service Q2 shr loss $0.18 vs $0.02.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Service Q2 shr loss $0.18 vs $0.02.</headline>
<dateline>NASHVILLE, Tenn. 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Service Merchandise Co Inc</p>
<p>Consolidated Statements of Operations</p>
<p>(unaudited)</p>
<p>					   Three Periods Ended (A)</p>
<p>						     ---------------</p>
<p>						   June 29   June 30</p>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)     1997	1996</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Net sales					877,361   859,984</p>
<p>Net loss					($17,547)  ($1,822)</p>
<p>								====================</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares and</p>
<p>  common share equivalents outstanding    99,900   101,527</p>
<p>Net loss per common share		    ($0.18)   ($0.02)</p>
<p>								====================</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>						     Six Months period</p>
<p>						     June 29   June 30</p>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)	 1997	1996</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Net sales				    1,563,761   1,575,612</p>
<p>Restructuring charge			 129,510	    -</p>
<p>Net loss				   ($124,764)   ($26,537)</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares and</p>
<p>common share equivalents outstanding  100,024     101,433</p>
<p>Net loss per common share		 ($1.25)     ($0.26)</p>
<p>(In thousands, except # of stores and selling days)</p>
<p>The second quarter ended June 29, 1997 contained 91 selling days versus the second quarter ended June 30, 1996 which contained 90 selling days. The six periods ended June 29, 1997 and June 30, 1996 each contained 181 selling days.</p>
<p>Restructuring charge related to the planned closure of 60 underperforming stores and the Company's Nevada distribution center.</p>
<p>1997 and 1996 per share data and number of shares include 497 and 524 shares of restricted stock, respectively.</p>
<p>The company said its net sales from operations was $762.1 million compared to $787.1 million.</p>
<p>The company said its second quarter share loss includes a charge of $0.19 per share which includes the $18.2 million after-tax impact related to facilities closing and remerchandising activities.</p>
